     "en": "Brahmagupta, an Indian mathematician of the 7th century, gave rules for adding and subtracting positive numbers (fortunes) and negative numbers (debts).\nExplorations: adding a negative number moves left on the number line and subtracting a negative moves right. The sum of a number and its opposite is zero.\nNegative numbers help us describe loss, depth and cold."
